  },
  "chapter": {
    "number": 77,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(78) A Psalm of",
          {
            "noteId": 139
          },
          "instruction for Asaph."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Give heed, O my people, to my law: incline your ear to the words of my mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will open my mouth in parables: I will utter dark sayings which have been from the beginning.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All which we have heard and known, and our fathers have declared to us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They were not hid from their children to a second generations; the fathers declaring the praises of the Lord, and his mighty acts, and his wonders which he wrought.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he raised up a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, to make it known to their children:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "that another generation might know, even the sons which should be born; and they should arise and declare them to their children.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "That they might set their hope on God, and not forget the works of God, but diligently seek his commandments.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "That they should not be as their fathers, a perverse and provoking generation; a generation which set not its heart aright, and its spirit was not",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 140
          },
          {
            "text": "steadfast with God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The children of Ephraim, bending and shooting with the bow, turned back in the day of battle.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They kept not the covenant of God, and would not walk in his law.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they forgot his benefits, and his miracles which he had showed them;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "the miracles which he wrought before their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the plain of Tanes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He clave the sea, and led them through: he made the waters to stand as in a bottle.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he guided them with a cloud by day, and all the night with a light of fire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "he clave a rock in the wilderness, and made them drink as in a great deep.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he brought water out of the rock, and caused waters to flow down as rivers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they sinned yet more against him; they provoked the Most High in the wilderness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they tempted God in their hearts, in asking meat for the desire of their souls.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They spoke also against God, and said, Will God be able to prepare a table in the wilderness?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Forasmuch as he struck the rock, and the waters flowed, and the torrents ran abundantly; will he be able also to give bread, or prepare a table for his people?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore the Lord heard, and was provoked: and fire was kindled in Jacob, and wrath went up against Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yet he commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and rained upon them manna to eat, and gave them the bread of heaven.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Man ate angels' bread; he sent them provision to the full.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He removed the south wind from heaven; and by his might he brought in the southwest wind.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he rained upon them flesh like dust, and feathered birds like the sand of the seas.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they fell into the midst of their camp, round about their tents.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So they ate, and were completely filled; and he gave them their desire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They were not disappointed of their desire: but when their food was yet in their mouth,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "then the indignation of God rose up against them, and killed the fattest of them, and overthrew the choice men of Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In the midst of all this they sinned yet more, and believed not his miracles.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And their days were consumed in vanity, and their years with anxiety.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When he killed them, they sought him: and they returned and called betimes upon God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they remembered that God was their helper, and the most high God was their redeemer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 36,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yet they loved him only with their mouth, and lied to him with their tongue.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 37,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For their heart was not right with him, neither were they steadfast in his covenant.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 38,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But he is compassionate, and will",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 141
          },
          {
            "text": "forgive their sins, and will not destroy them: yes, he will frequently turn away his wrath, and will not kindle all his anger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 39,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he remembered that they are flesh; a wind that passes away, and returns not.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 40,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How often did they provoke him in the wilderness, and anger him in a dry land!",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 41,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yes, they turned back, and tempted God, and provoked the Holy One of Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 42,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They remembered not his hand, the day in which he delivered them from the hand of the oppressor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 43,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How he had wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Tanes:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 44,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and had changed their rivers into blood; and their",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 142
          },
          {
            "text": "streams, that they should not drink.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 45,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent against them the dog-fly, and it devoured them; and the frog, and it spoiled them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 46,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he gave their fruit to the canker worm, and their labors to the locust.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 47,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He killed their vines with hail, and their sycamores with frost.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 48,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he gave up their cattle to hail, and their substance to the fire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 49,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent out against them the fury of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and affliction, a message by evil angels.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 50,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He made a way for his wrath; he spared not their souls from death, but consigned their cattle to death;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 51,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and struck every firstborn in the land of Egypt; the first fruits of their labors in the tents of Cham.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 52,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he removed his people like sheep; he led them as a flock in the wilderness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 53,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he guided them with hope, and they feared not: but the sea covered their enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 54,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he brought them in to the mountain of his sanctuary, this mountain which his right hand had purchased.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 55,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he cast out the nations from before them, and made them to inherit by a line of inheritance, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 56,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and kept not his testimonies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 57,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they turned back, and broke covenant, even as also their fathers: they became like a crooked bow.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 58,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they provoked him with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 59,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God heard and",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 143
          },
          {
            "text": "lightly regarded them, and greatly despised Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 60,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he rejected the tabernacle of Selom, his tent where he lived among men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 61,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he gave their strength into captivity, and their beauty into the enemy's hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 62,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 144
          },
          {
            "text": "gave his people to the sword; and disdained his inheritance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 63,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fire devoured their young men; and their virgins mourned not.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 64,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows shall not be wept for.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 65,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So the Lord awaked as one out of sleep, and as a mighty man who has been heated with wine.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 66,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he struck his enemies in the hinder parts: he brought on them a perpetual reproach.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 67,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he rejected the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 68,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "but chose the tribe of Juda, the mount Sion which he loved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 69,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he built his sanctuary as the place of unicorns; he founded it for ever on the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 70,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He chose David also his servant, and took him up from the flocks of sheep.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 71,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He took him from following the ewes great with young, to be the shepherd of Jacob his servant, and Israel his inheritance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 72,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So he tended them in the innocency of his heart; and guided them by the skillfulness of his hands.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 139,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. understanding.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 140,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, faithfully secured.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 8
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 141,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. be propitious, or, merciful to.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 38
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 142,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. rains, or, showers.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 44
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 143,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. overlooked them. See Acts 17:30.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 59
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 144,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. shut up.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 77,
          "verse": 62
        }
      }
